-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Exemption) (No. 2) Order (G.N. No. S 591/2002; O 2, 2004 Revised Edition, amended by S 212/2022), made under s 60(b) of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-exemption-no-2-order-2002/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-OR2.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- It exempts four named broadcasting holding companies from section 33 of the Act. Dated: the window of the Order as deposited.
-- S 212/2022, the Order that deleted sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph 2, is deposited and encoded in `sgba-i-s212-2022.l4`; the text of O 2 before it is not held, and `sgba-versions-acts.l4` reads O 2 on two days (the day of the conduct, the day the law is read as at).

§ `Paragraph 2: Exemption`

-- src:4 | Exemption
-- src:5 | 2. The Minister hereby exempts the following broadcasting holding companies from section 33 of the Act:
-- src:6 | ( a ) [ Deleted by S 212/2022 wef 25/03/2022 ]
-- src:7 | ( b ) Singapore Technologies Pte Ltd;
-- src:8 | ( c ) Singapore Technologies Telemedia Pte Ltd;
-- src:9 | ( d ) STT Communications Ltd; and
@ref para 2(a) to (e) (src:4-9)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      name IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`O 2 para 2 the company is exempt from section 33 of the Act, on` MEANS
    IF `the Exemption (No. 2) Order as deposited is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (name EQUALS "Singapore Technologies Pte Ltd" OR name EQUALS "Singapore Technologies Telemedia Pte Ltd" OR name EQUALS "STT Communications Ltd" OR name EQUALS "Temasek Holdings (Private) Limited")
    ELSE NOTHING
